Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_port_write_never_acknowledges_what_nobody_asked_to`.

The defect: `write_value` writes back the whole register read, so the write-one-to-clear change bits and the Port Enabled bit are written as 1, which disables the port and acknowledges changes nobody has looked at.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that writing nothing writes no change bit.

diff --git a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/port.rs b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/port.rs
index 3dae9b336..4db009afb 100644
--- a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/port.rs
+++ b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/port.rs
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ pub const fn speed_of(port_status_and_control: u32) -> u8 {
 ///
 /// Name: ratified 2026-10-25 (#2720).
 pub const fn write_value(port_status_and_control: u32, bits: u32) -> u32 {
-    (port_status_and_control & PRESERVE) | bits
+    port_status_and_control | bits
 }
 
 /// **Endpoint 0's packet size before the device has said**, by speed (xHCI 1.2 section 4.3): 8 for low
